  "reason": "Bind await tighter than the power operator, so `await f() ** 2` groups as `(await f()) ** 2` instead of `await (f() ** 2)`. Six patch corpus trees, one pinned kit input (`r = await f() ** 2`, alt-python-B02-05 step 0) and fourteen seeded edits of the patch corpus change. Each previously error-free fresh tree changes only by the documented fix: an `await` whose operand held the following `**` expression now ends before the operator, and that `binary_operator` takes the `await` as its left operand. Of the fourteen edits, three (001-e1, 006-e2, 009-e3) are error-free before and after, and eleven have an error tree in both builds (003-e1 differs only in its changed ranges). Every other pinned upstream corpus tree and edit, the three pinned large inputs and every other previously error-free tree in this comparison are unchanged.",
  "retireWhen": "An approved Python pin contains a fix for the await and power-operator binding defect reported in upstream PR #360. The pin move updates the patch corpus expectations.",
